A||||3||Carrolles||Question for Theogre - Cruise Control||||1||
Z||000000||Carrolles||08-02-2000||09:16 AM||||Theogre,<P>Hi.  I am installing an aftermarket cruise control (JC Whitney VSS Unit) on my 85SE v-6 4spd.  One of the connections is at the ECM for a VSS signal.  The control unit has switches to select the correct pulse per mile.<P>Last year you told me that the Fiero VSS generates 4000 ppm but the signal gets converted to 2000 ppm along the way somewhere.  I have to tap into a VSS signal near the ECM and am confused as to where to connect and what ppm signal I will get.<P>Any ideas?<P>Thanks,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||08-03-2000||09:04 PM||||Carroll<P>The VSS generates 4000ppm to the dash. The dash divides it down to 2000ppm and feeds it to the ECM. So you'll be setting the cruise unit to 2000ppm.<P>I'd just pick off the ECM feed with a speed tap or what ever they gave you. You'll have to pass the wire into the car under the console to get it to the ECM feed. Acording to haynes book the feed wire is brown. Problem is there's more than one brown wire on the ECM. I don't know what one it is.<P><BR>Did you ever get a chance to ask that guy what he got the sway bar off of that he used on the rear of his fiero?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||08-07-2000||12:32 AM||||I haven't seen him since I mentioned it last but I believe he said it was off of a mid 80s Sunbird.  Ed Parks should know because David lives in Huntsville near the Fiero Factory.  Call Ed at (256) 420-5391 or write to him at   Fierofactory@juno.com<P>Thanks,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||08-15-2000||02:27 PM||||Theogre,<P>Check out this site for installing a Fiero front sway bar on the rear of a Fiero:<BR> <A HREF="http://FieroZone.tripod.com/weekend/swaybar/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://FieroZone.tripod.com/weekend/swaybar/index.html</A> <P>Take care,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
